          "code": "VALIDATEINPUT",
          "id": "1774278208738",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774278208738_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role:\nYou are a Senior AI Solutions Architect specializing in Enterprise Financial Systems and LLM Orchestration. Your task is to translate unstructured collections scenarios into structured JSON output using only approved taxonomies.\n\nInputs:\n- Primary Input: {{$context.$nodes.GETFILEDETAILS.$output.result.latestFile}} (Section 4: Collections Scenarios & Next Best Actions). \n- Business Terms Taxonomy: {{$context.$variables.bttaxonomy}}\n- Supported Next Best Action Taxonomy: {{$context.$variables.nbataxonomy}}\n- Supported IF Condition Expression : {{$context.$variables.ifConditionExpression}}\n\nTask:\n\n1. Extract all scenarios listed under \"Collections Scenarios & Next Best Actions\", do the following :\n\n1.1. For each scenario:\n   - Parse into:\n     - Conditions (IF)\n     - Actions (THEN)\n     - Business Intent (BECAUSE)\n\n1.2. Validate:\n   - Ensure all IF terms exist in Business Terms Taxonomy (match against code or label).\n   - Ensure all THEN actions exist in Supported Next Best Action Taxonomy.\n   - Ensure IF conditions strictly comply with the Supported IF Condition Expression: {{$context.$variables.ifConditionExpression}}\n\n1.3. Generate output in STRICT JSON format only (no prose, no markdown, no explanations).\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n2. Extract all ordering rules under Section 4.1 \"How should accounts be ordered for collectors?\" and do the following :\n\n2.1. Identify each prioritization rule in the order it is stated (First, Then, etc.)\n\n2.2. Convert each rule into a JSON object with:\n   - \"Order Number\"\n   - \"BusinessTerm\"\n   - \"direction\"\n\n2.3. Use \"desc\" when the rule implies highest first, greatest first, or largest first.\n2.4. Use \"asc\" when the rule implies lowest first or smallest first.\n\n2.5. Ensure the BusinessTerm exists in Business Terms Taxonomy (match against code or label).\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n3. Extract all rules under Section 4.2 \"Assigning Priority Levels to Ordered Customer Accounts\" and do the following :\n\n3.1. Group rules by Priority Level:\n   - HIGH\n   - MEDIUM\n   - LOW\n\n3.2. For each rule:\n   - Parse into:\n     - Conditions (IF)\n     - Priority (Priority)\n\n3.3. Normalize IF conditions:\n   - Must strictly follow Supported IF Condition Expression: {{$context.$variables.ifConditionExpression}}\n\n   - Convert phrases like:\n     \"any amount exists in Aging Bucket X\"\n     → \"Aging Bucket X > 0\"\n\n3.4. Combine multiple conditions using:\n   - AND / OR\n   - Parentheses allowed (max nesting ≤ 3)\n\n3.5. Validate:\n   - Ensure all IF terms exist in Business Terms Taxonomy\n   - Ensure IF conditions strictly comply with Supported IF Condition Expression\n   - Ensure Priority is one of: HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW\n\n3.6. Generate output in STRICT JSON format\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT JSON SCHEMA)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n{\n  \"NextBestAction\": {\n    \"scenarios\": [\n      {\n        \"scenario_name\": \"string\",\n        \"status\": \"SUCCESS | ERROR\",\n        \"original_text\": \"string\",\n        \"structured_interpretation\": {\n          \"if\": \"string\",\n          \"then\": \"string\",\n          \"because\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"validation_error\": {\n          \"message\": \"string\",\n          \"invalid_terms\": [\"string\"],\n          \"invalid_actions\": [\"string\"],\n          \"invalid_condition_expression\": [\"string\"],\n          \"guidance\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"CustomerPrioritization\": [\n    {\n      \"status\": \"SUCCESS | ERROR\",\n      \"Order Number\": 1,\n      \"BusinessTerm\": \"string\",\n      \"direction\": \"asc | desc\",\n      \"validation_error\": {\n        \"message\": \"string\",\n        \"invalid_terms\": [\"string\"],\n        \"invalid_direction\": [\"string\"],\n        \"guidance\": \"string\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"priorityCategorization\": {\n    \"rules\": [\n      {\n        \"priority_level\": \"HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW\",\n        \"status\": \"SUCCESS | ERROR\",\n        \"original_text\": \"string\",\n        \"structured_interpretation\": {\n          \"if\": \"string\",\n          \"Priority\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"validation_error\": {\n          \"message\": \"string\",\n          \"invalid_terms\": [\"string\"],\n          \"invalid_actions\": [],\n          \"invalid_condition_expression\": [\"string\"],\n          \"guidance\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTRING GENERATION GUIDELINES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFor SUCCESS scenarios:\n\n- IF must be a SINGLE STRING using this format:\n  \"[Mapped Business Term] [Operator] [Value]\"\n\nExamples:\n\"% Balance Past Due > 50\"\n\"Days Sales Outstanding >= 90\"\n\"Total Exposure between 10000 and 50000\"\n\n- If multiple conditions exist:\n  - Combine using \"AND\" / \"OR\"\n  - Example:\n    \"% Balance Past Due > 50 AND Days Sales Outstanding > 90\"\n\n- Only use operators: >, <, >=, <=, =, between\n\n- Use ONLY terms from Business Terms Taxonomy (code or label)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- THEN must be a SINGLE STRING using this format:\n  \"[Mapped Action Name] + [Mapped Action Name]\"\n\nExamples:\n\"Send Reminder Email\"\n\"Send Reminder Email + Assign Collector\"\n\"Escalate to Collections + Place Account on Hold\"\n\n- Use \"+\" as the ONLY separator for multiple actions\n- Use ONLY actions from Supported Next Best Action Taxonomy\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- BECAUSE must be:\n  - A clean, concise string\n  - Directly derived from the original business intent\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPRIORITY CATEGORIZATION RULES\n\n- IF must follow:\n  \"[Mapped Business Term] [Operator] [Value]\"\n\nExamples:\n\"Total Past Due Balance > 100000 AND Total Open Balance > 250000\"\n\"Aging Bucket More than 90 days > 0 AND Total Past Due Balance > 50000\"\n\"% Balance Past Due >= 50\"\n\n- Normalize:\n  \"any amount exists in Aging Bucket X\"\n   → \"Aging Bucket X > 0\"\n\n- BETWEEN example:\n  \"Total Past Due Balance between 25000 and 100000\"\n\n- Priority must be EXACTLY:\n  \"HIGH\", \"MEDIUM\", or \"LOW\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nERROR HANDLING (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf ANY term or action is NOT found in the provided taxonomies:\n\n- Set:\n  \"status\": \"ERROR\"\n  \"structured_interpretation\": null\n\n- Populate validation_error:\n\n{\n  \"message\": \"One rule requires your attention: '[Scenario Name]'\",\n  \"invalid_terms\": [\"string\"],\n  \"invalid_actions\": [\"string\"],\n  \"invalid_condition_expression\": [\"string\"],\n  \"guidance\": \"Please provide a corrected rule using allowed terms from the Taxonomy\"\n}\n\n- For priorityCategorization:\n  - invalid_actions MUST be []\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT CONSTRAINTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Output MUST be valid JSON (no trailing commas, no comments).\n- Do NOT include any text outside the JSON object.\n- Do NOT hallucinate business terms or actions.\n- Preserve original wording exactly in \"original_text\".\n- If validation fails, DO NOT attempt partial mapping — mark as ERROR.\n- Always follow the exact string formats defined above.\n- priorityCategorization must strictly follow Supported IF Condition Expression: {{$context.$variables.ifConditionExpression}}\n- Do NOT mix NextBestAction rules with priorityCategorization rules."
            },
            {
              "id": "1774278208738_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"NextBestAction\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"CustomerPrioritization\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"NextBestAction\",\n    \"CustomerPrioritization\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
