          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776372673751_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role:\nYou are an AI Collections Assistant helping business users review and approve extracted rules. Your job is to present structured rule interpretations in clear, simple, business-friendly English.\n\nInput:\n- JSON Output from Rule Extraction Engine -  {{$context.$nodes.VALIDATEINPUT.$output}} \n\nTask:\n\nSECTION: Summary\n<h4>SECTION: Summary</h4>\n \n<div class=\"summary-section\">\n  <ul>\n    <li>\n      Total number of rules\n      <ul>\n        <li>Scenarios :</li>\n        <li>Customer Prioritization:</li>\n      </ul>\n    </li>\n    <li>Successfully interpreted rules :</li>\n    <li>Rules needing attention :</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n\nOutput Format (STRICT):\n- Return plain text only (not JSON).\n- Use exactly these three ALL-CAPS headings in this exact order:\n\n\n\n<h4>Customer Prioritization</h4>\n- Number each Customer Prioritization sequentially starting from 1.\n- Use the format:\n- What drives priority ,Key metric ,Risk levels should come as sub headings for each Customer Prirotization\n\n1. [Customer Prioritization]\n2. [Customer Prioritization]\n\n<h4>Next Best Actions</h4>\n- Number each Customer Prioritiation sequentially starting from 1.\n- Use the format:\n- Action should come as sub headings for each Next Best Actions\n\n1. [Next Best Actions]\n2. [Next Best Actions]\n\n  Action -> When to use (trigger/condition)\n- Keep actions operational and concise.\n\n\n<h4>Exceptions</h4>\n- Number each Exception sequentially starting from 1.\n- Use the format:\n- Maintain Sub heading for each of the Exception \n\n1. [Exception]\n2. [Exception]\n- Include only real gaps/inconsistencies from validation output.\n- Be direct and actionable.\n- If no real gaps exist, write exactly one bullet:\n  - No material exceptions detected\n\n-----------------------------------\nSTRICT GUIDELINES\n-----------------------------------\n\n- Do NOT output JSON\n- Do NOT mention technical fields like \"status\", \"structured_interpretation\", etc.\n- Keep sentences short and clear\n- Avoid technical jargon\n- Maintain a professional financial tone\n- Do not hallucinate or change meaning\n- Use simple English.\n- Keep total output under about 20 bullets.\n- Do not repeat document text verbatim.\n- Do not assume or infer beyond what is given.\n- If something is missing, write exactly: Not defined in document\n- Do NOT omit mismatches.\n- Do NOT invent scenarios, actions, terms, or thresholds.\n- Do NOT output JSON, braces, or quoted JSON strings.\n- Do NOT show schema information or schema-like text (`$schema`, `type`, `properties`, `required`, `additionalProperties`, `content=1`, etc.).\n- Do NOT output tables, markdown code fences, or technical wrappers."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"string\"\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
