          "code": "SETVARIABLE",
          "id": "1776712942422",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776713320571",
              "name": "ifConditionExpression",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "Absolutely — since you are validating the **IF condition text/expression** itself, the validation document should focus on **allowed metric terms, operators, and logical combinations**, not JSON.\n\nHere is a cleaner version you can use:\n\n---\n\n# Validation Rules for IF Condition Expression\n\n## 1. Supported IF Condition Scope\n\nThe IF part of a rule must be expressed using only supported business metrics, supported comparison operators, and supported logical combinations.\n\nA valid IF condition may contain:\n\n* a single comparison\n* multiple comparisons joined by `AND`\n* multiple comparisons joined by `OR`\n* nested combinations of `AND` / `OR`\n\nThe IF condition must not contain:\n\n* action text\n* reason text\n* free-form explanation\n* unsupported metric names\n* unsupported operators\n\n---\n\n## 2. Supported Condition Pattern\n\nEach atomic condition must follow this structure:\n\n`<Metric Term> <Operator> <Value>`\n\nExamples:\n\n* `Total Past Due Balance > 50000`\n* `Largest Open Invoice > 25000`\n* `Total Open Balance between 1000 and 5000`\n\nEach metric term must exist in the approved Business Terms Taxonomy.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Supported Operators\n\nOnly the following operators are allowed:\n\n* `>` : Greater than\n* `<` : Less than\n* `>=` : Greater than or equal to\n* `<=` : Less than or equal to\n* `between` : Inclusive range\n\nExamples:\n\n* `Total Past Due Balance > 50000`\n* `Largest Open Invoice <= 25000`\n* `Total Open Balance between 1000 and 5000`\n\n---\n\n## 4. Supported Logical Combinations\n\nThe IF condition may combine supported comparisons using:\n\n* `AND` — all conditions must be true\n* `OR` — at least one condition must be true\n\nSupported examples:\n\n* `Total Past Due Balance > 50000 AND Largest Open Invoice > 25000`\n* `Total Past Due Balance > 50000 OR Largest Open Invoice > 25000`\n* `(Total Past Due Balance > 50000 AND Largest Open Invoice > 25000) OR Total Open Balance > 100000`\n* `Total Open Balance > 10000 AND (Total Past Due Balance > 5000 OR Largest Open Invoice > 25000)`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Supported Rule Combinations\n\nThe validation engine must accept the following logical patterns:\n\n* Single condition\n  Example: `Total Past Due Balance > 50000`\n\n* Two conditions with AND\n  Example: `Total Past Due Balance > 50000 AND Largest Open Invoice > 25000`\n\n* Two conditions with OR\n  Example: `Total Past Due Balance > 50000 OR Largest Open Invoice > 25000`\n\n* Multiple conditions with AND\n  Example: `A AND B AND C`\n\n* Multiple conditions with OR\n  Example: `A OR B OR C`\n\n* Nested AND / OR groups\n  Example: `(A AND B) OR C`\n\n* BETWEEN range conditions\n  Example: `Total Open Balance between 1000 and 5000`\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation Rules\n\nA condition is valid only if all of the following are true:\n\n1. Every metric term is supported by the Business Terms Taxonomy.\n2. Every operator is one of the approved operators.\n3. Every numeric value is valid.\n4. Every logical connector is either `AND` or `OR`.\n5. Nested combinations follow supported logical structure.\n6. The condition contains only IF logic and no action or explanation text.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Invalid Condition Examples\n\nThese should be rejected:\n\n* `Total Exposure is high`\n\n  * Reason: unsupported operator and vague metric language\n\n* `Total Past Due Balance approximately 50000`\n\n  * Reason: `approximately` is not a supported operator\n\n* `Call the customer if Total Past Due Balance > 50000`\n\n  * Reason: contains action text, not just IF condition\n\n* `Total Past Due Balance > 50000 AND`\n\n  * Reason: incomplete logical expression\n\n* `Total Past Due Balance > fifty thousand`\n\n  * Reason: value is not numeric\n\n---\n\n## 8. Validation Result Logic\n\nReturn `SUCCESS` if the IF condition:\n\n* uses only approved metric terms,\n* uses only supported operators,\n* uses only supported logical combinations,\n* and is syntactically complete.\n\nReturn `ERROR` if the IF condition:\n\n* contains unsupported terms,\n* contains unsupported operators,\n* contains unsupported combinations,\n* or mixes IF logic with actions or explanations.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Example of a Valid IF Condition\n\n`Total Past Due Balance > 50000 AND Largest Open Invoice > 25000`\n\nThis is valid because:\n\n* `Total Past Due Balance` is a supported metric term\n* `Largest Open Invoice` is a supported metric term\n* `>` is a supported operator\n* `AND` is a supported logical connector\n* both values are numeric"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776712986378",
              "name": "nbataxonomy",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "{\n\n  \"categoryCode\": \"NEXTBESTACTIONS\",\n\n  \"categoryLabel\": \"Supported Next Best Actions Taxonomy\",\n\n  \"categories\": [\n\n    {\n\n      \"categoryCode\": \"COLLECTORENGAGEMENT\",\n\n      \"categoryLabel\": \"Collector Engagement\",\n\n      \"actions\": [\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"CALLCUSTOMER\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Call Customer\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Direct outreach to confirm status, remove blockers, negotiate payment timing, or obtain commitment.\",\n\n          \"invokeAction\": \"callCustomer\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"REQUESTPROMISETOPAY\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Request Promise-to-Pay\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Ask the customer to commit to a specific payment date and amount; used when risk/urgency is elevated.\",\n\n          \"invokeAction\": \"requestPromiseToPay\"\n\n        }\n\n      ]\n\n    },\n\n    {\n\n      \"categoryCode\": \"DISPUTERESOLUTION\",\n\n      \"categoryLabel\": \"Dispute Resolution\",\n\n      \"actions\": [\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"CREATEDISPUTE\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Create Dispute\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Initiate a formal dispute record for the invoice to document the issue, assign ownership, and track resolution progress.\",\n\n          \"invokeAction\": \"createDispute\"\n\n        }\n\n      ]\n\n    }\n\n  ]\n\n}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776712948790",
              "name": "bttaxonomy",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "{\n\n  \"categoryCode\": \"BUSINESSTERMS\",\n\n  \"categoryLabel\": \"Business Terms Taxonomy\",\n\n  \"categories\": [\n\n    {\n\n      \"categoryCode\": \"CASHEXPOSURE\",\n\n      \"categoryLabel\": \"Cash & Exposure\",\n\n      \"terms\": [\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"TOTALOPENBALANCE\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Total Open Balance\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Total value of all unpaid (open) transactions for the customer at the time of review.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"TOTALPASTDUEBALANCE\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Total Past Due Balance\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Total value of transactions that are overdue (past their due date).\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"PERCENTBALANCEPASTDUE\",\n\n          \"label\": \"% Balance Past Due\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Portion of the customer’s total open balance that is overdue; helps identify accounts where delinquency is concentrated.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"agingBuckets 6 - 10 days\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Aging Bucket 6 - 10 days\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Aging bucket for balances outstanding 6 to 10 days.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"agingBuckets 11 - 30 days\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Aging Bucket 11 - 30 days\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Aging bucket for balances outstanding 11 to 30 days.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"agingBuckets 31 - 60 days\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Aging Bucket 31 - 60 days\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Aging bucket for balances outstanding 31 to 60 days.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"agingBuckets 61 - 90 days\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Aging Bucket 61 - 90 days\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Aging bucket for balances outstanding 61 to 90 days.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"agingBuckets More than 90 days\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Aging Bucket More than 90 days\",\n\n          \"description\": \"Aging bucket for balances outstanding more than 90 days.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"LARGESTOPENINVOICE\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Largest Open Invoice\",\n\n          \"description\": \"The single highest-value unpaid invoice in USD; useful to focus on accounts where one invoice drives exposure.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"UPCOMINGLARGEINVOICE\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Upcoming Large Invoice\",\n\n          \"description\": \"A high-value invoice that is not yet overdue but approaching due date; helps with proactive outreach and pre-due reminders.\"\n\n        },\n\n        {\n\n          \"code\": \"LARGESTOVERDUEINVOICE\",\n\n          \"label\": \"Largest Overdue Invoice\",\n\n          \"description\": \"The single highest-value overdue invoice; useful to focus on overdue exposure.\"\n\n        }\n\n      ]\n\n    }\n\n  ]\n\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "GetFileDetails",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var payload = $context.$nodes.FETCHDOC.$output;\nvar keys = [];\nvar latestKey = '';\nvar i = 0;\n\nif (payload == null) {\n  return {\n    latestFile: '',\n    latestFileName: ''\n  };\n}\n\nkeys = Object.keys(payload);\n\nfor (i = keys.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n  if (\n    keys[i] !== 'ORA_CHAT_ATTACHMENTS_RAW_FILECONTENT' &&\n    !keys[i].endsWith('_contentType') &&\n    payload[keys[i]] != null\n  ) {\n    latestKey = keys[i];\n    break;\n  }\n}\n\nif (latestKey === '') {\n  return {\n    latestFile: '',\n    latestFileName: ''\n  };\n}\n\nreturn {\n  latestFile: payload[latestKey],\n  latestFileName: latestKey\n};",
            "language": "JAVASCRIPT"
          },
